Package: voice-type
Version: 0.3.1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, libgtk-4-1, libnotify-bin, pipewire-bin, pkexec
Recommends: ydotool
Maintainer: Kang Feipeng <269406200+kangfp@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Voice dictation for Ubuntu GNOME Wayland
 Hold right Alt and speak; recognized text is streamed into the focused app
 segment by segment as recognition proceeds.
 Local recognition uses faster-whisper (models downloaded from Hugging Face,
 hf-mirror or ModelScope, chosen in a first-run wizard); an OpenAI-compatible
 online API can be used instead. Includes a GTK4/libadwaita control window
 with settings, hotkey registration and environment diagnostics.
 Bundles wl-copy/wl-paste (GPL-3+, see wl-clipboard.copyright) so no
 secondary clipboard package install is needed.
